      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Definition of Article"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Articles are demonstrative adjectives classified into Indefinite (A, An) and Definite (The).",
        "'A' is used before singular countable nouns beginning with a consonant sound, regardless of the spelling (e.g., a university, a one-rupee note).",
        "'An' is used before singular countable nouns beginning with a vowel sound (e.g., an hour, an M.L.A.).",
        "'The' specifies a particular person, place, or thing, and is used before unique natural objects, geographical features, and superlative adjectives.",
        "Articles must be omitted before abstract nouns, uncountable nouns, proper nouns, and names of languages or sports under general contexts."
      ],
      "id": "t34fg7k"
    },
